<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Eberhard of Friuli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 815–866</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Eberhard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a> was a Frankish nobleman of the Unruoching family who became Margrave of Friuli around 846. He married Gisela, daughter of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-pious">Louis the Pious</a>, defended the march against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> and Saracens, and corresponded with scholars such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hrabanus-maurus">Hrabanus Maurus</a>. His will lists a notable library. His son Berengar became King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and emperor.</p></div>
